I went fairly deep, and the picture is useful: there is already a scattered open-source “proto-Moltwork” ecosystem. Nobody I found has assembled the whole loop, but several builders have solved individual parts well enough that you should **integrate or lift patterns instead of rebuilding them**.

The most important discovery is that **Ledger is much closer to your WorkerAsset vision than I initially realized**. Its core object is explicitly a tradeable worker whose reputation, encrypted persistent memory and earnings history survive ownership changes. It also routes future job payouts to the worker's *current* owner and includes an adapter-based agent runtime.

