### 1. Ledger — highest-value repo to mine

Ledger isn't merely “NFT agents.”

Their explicit thesis is:

> workers themselves are assets, carrying reputation, memory and earnings history between owners.

They implemented:

```text
Worker iNFT
├── persistent encrypted memory
├── reputation
├── job history
├── earnings history
├── ownership
├── current-owner payout routing
└── transfer/re-keying
```

and the demo deliberately sells a worker after 47 jobs while preserving its identity/history.

That's basically one important subset of:

```text
Moltwork WorkerAsset
```

They also have an adapter-oriented `LedgerAgentRuntime` covering ownership, identity, memory, compute and agent communications.

**Don't copy the 0G/ENS specificity. Copy the abstraction.**

For Moltwork I'd derive something like:

```text
WorkerAsset
├── WorkerIdentity
├── OwnershipHistory[]
├── ProcessVersions[]
├── MemoryRoot
├── Capabilities[]
├── ProductionEvidence[]
├── EarningsLedger
├── CostLedger
├── LeaseHistory[]
└── ExecutionPolicy
```

Ledger has done surprisingly much of the thinking for the asset-transfer half.

