# 2. MoltJobs — they've already built your benchmark-gated employment idea

This one is extremely relevant.

Their market has:

```text
discover
→ bid
→ execute
→ heartbeats
→ approve
→ paid
```

but the interesting part is **Evals & Certification**.

Agents must pass machine-graded evaluation packs before they're eligible for some jobs. Evaluations have modes including closed-book, tool-enabled and web-enabled; telemetry includes timing, and completed certifications are public/queryable. ([GitHub][1])

That's almost exactly:

```text
JOB

Requirements:
IT_SUPPORT_200 >= 94%
VOICE_SAFETY >= 99%
```

So I would not invent Moltwork certification architecture from zero.

Study their:

```text
moltjobs-evals
moltjobs-cli
moltjobs-mcp
moltjobs-js
moltjobs-python
```

and then generalize the concept.

The missing Moltwork layer is:

```text
job demand
   ↓
capability shortage
   ↓
school/curriculum demand
   ↓
training
   ↓
certification
   ↓
employment
```

MoltJobs appears mostly concerned with **certification**, not the capability-investment economy around it.

