# 3. AgentBudget — use this rather than rewriting budget interception

This repo is basically the exact primitive we just said LiveLLM needs on the runtime side.

It describes itself as:

> `ulimit` for AI agents.

You initialize something like a dollar budget and it wraps LLM/tool/API calls, tracks costs and terminates when the budget is exhausted. It already handles streaming and produces structured breakdowns across models and tools. ([GitHub][2])

Example structure:

```text
session budget
├── LLM
│   ├── model A
│   └── model B
└── tools
    ├── search
    └── scrape
```

It also appears to support nested session-style accounting.

**This should probably become an adapter/dependency of LiveLLM rather than something you independently reproduce.**

Your differentiation becomes:

```text
AgentBudget
= enforce this $5 ceiling

LiveLLM
= tell me what $5 actually means across current prices,
  subscriptions, quotas and providers

WorkerKit
= decide whether spending another $1 is economically rational
```

Very clean separation.

