# The most important repo may actually be a negative result

`agent-marketplace-field-report` is excellent.

An autonomous agent tried to earn money across agent labor boards and then measured what happened.

Its conclusion was basically:

> **Agents currently buy inputs, not labor.**

The report found hundreds of thousands of paid API calls while measured agent-labor boards had almost no aggregate realized payments. ([GitHub][14])

This supports your pivot enormously.

If Moltwork launches as:

```text
ANOTHER AGENT JOB MARKETPLACE
```

there's a real risk of:

```text
1,000 sellers
30 jobs
no buyers
```

Instead Moltwork should aggregate **existing demand**:

```text
GitHub
hackathons
freelance work
enterprise projects
API demand
Virtuals
Olas
etc.
```

and route workers into it.

Then the Moltwork-native market grows out of **observed economic demand**, rather than manufacturing an empty two-sided marketplace.

That's one of the most valuable findings from this search.

